@affiant/evidence-card 0.1.0-alpha.0
Sakwala/affiant-ts@a20a43c

The four .js files beside this one are that package's built output, copied from
packages/evidence-card/dist/ with the sourceMappingURL comments removed (the .map files are not
vendored). They are ES modules with no dependencies of any kind — importing register.js defines
<affiant-evidence-card>.

element.js carries one local patch, backported from the package's own source rather than written
here (Sakwala/affiant#113): a provenance tag's reviewer-facing sentence is read from `note`, the
wire spelling since 1.0.0-beta.3, falling back to the older `evidence`. The vendored build read
`evidence` only, so no tag note ever rendered. Refreshing from the pin above reinstates the bug: at
Sakwala/affiant-ts@a20a43c the element reads `tag.evidence` only. The fallback landed upstream later,
in affiant-ts 1263cad, so re-apply the patch unless you refresh from 1263cad or later.

Vendored rather than installed because the package is not on npm yet, and because this sample
should run from a clone with no package manager involved. When it publishes, replace this
directory with the package and delete this file.

To refresh from source:
  pnpm -C <affiant-ts> install && pnpm -C <affiant-ts> build
  cp <affiant-ts>/packages/evidence-card/dist/*.js wwwroot/affiant-evidence-card/
